within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EX02_Sorafenib;
model Sorafenib "Sorafenib — default model: Sorafenib_Jain2011_reference"
  extends Sorafenib_Jain2011_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of sorafenib: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EX02_Sorafenib.Sorafenib_Jain2011_reference\">Sorafenib_Jain2011_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of sorafenib in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Sorafenib_Jain2011_reference</code></li><li><code>Sorafenib_Choi2021_PD_tumor_growth_inhibition</code></li></ul><h4>About sorafenib</h4><p>Sorafenib is an anticancer protein kinase inhibitor used to treat liver cancer (hepatocellular carcinoma) and kidney cancer (renal cell carcinoma), and it has also been studied for other cancers such as thyroid cancer and acute myeloid leukemia. It is authorised in the European Union and widely used in cancer care.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421136\">Wikidata Q421136</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Sorafenib\">Sorafenib</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 345600, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Sorafenib;
